{
  "schema_version": "1.0",
  "encounter_id": "00593",
  "segments": [
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0001",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 0.63,
      "end_seconds": 9.17,
      "duration_seconds": 8.54,
      "text": "Hello, doctor. I'm here for the hep C follow-up, I think? The letter wasn't very clear about it."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0002",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 11.53,
      "end_seconds": 28.01,
      "duration_seconds": 16.48,
      "text": "That's right. You finished your course of treatment in the spring, so today is about how you are and what we check next. How are you feeling in yourself?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0003",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 28.88,
      "end_seconds": 34.7,
      "duration_seconds": 5.82,
      "text": "Better, mostly. I mean, tired, I'd say. Still tired, if I'm honest."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0004",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 37.22,
      "end_seconds": 44.91,
      "duration_seconds": 7.69,
      "text": "How tired, and is it there all day or only at certain times?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0005",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 46.16,
      "end_seconds": 56.12,
      "duration_seconds": 9.96,
      "text": "Most afternoons I just hit a wall. Heavy, sort of, I can't explain it better than that."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0006",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 59.08,
      "end_seconds": 64.38,
      "duration_seconds": 5.3,
      "text": "Anything else you've noticed since you finished the treatment?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0007",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 66.96,
      "end_seconds": 72.06,
      "duration_seconds": 5.1,
      "text": "My joints are achy, knees and hands mostly."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0008",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 73.72,
      "end_seconds": 76.96,
      "duration_seconds": 3.24,
      "text": "When did that start?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0009",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 79.15,
      "end_seconds": 86.91,
      "duration_seconds": 7.76,
      "text": "Oh, I couldn't tell you. It crept up on me, I've no idea when it began."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0010",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 89.75,
      "end_seconds": 96.29,
      "duration_seconds": 6.54,
      "text": "Fair enough, that's very common. What about your tummy, any trouble there?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0011",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 97.54,
      "end_seconds": 104.13,
      "duration_seconds": 6.59,
      "text": "Now and then I feel queasy after fatty stuff, a fry-up or a takeaway."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0012",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 105.62,
      "end_seconds": 112.66,
      "duration_seconds": 7.04,
      "text": "Is your skin or the whites of your eyes looking yellow at all?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0013",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 113.95,
      "end_seconds": 120.73,
      "duration_seconds": 6.78,
      "text": "No, nothing like that. I'd have noticed, and so would the lads at work."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0014",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 123.01,
      "end_seconds": 132.21,
      "duration_seconds": 9.2,
      "text": "Good. Lie back for me and I'll have a feel of your tummy and look at your ankles. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0015",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 134.46,
      "end_seconds": 140.46,
      "duration_seconds": 6.0,
      "text": "Okay, go on. Sorry, cold hands! I mean you, not me. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0016",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 156.07,
      "end_seconds": 164.21,
      "duration_seconds": 8.14,
      "text": "Your tummy is soft with no tenderness, and your ankles look fine, no swelling."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0017",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 165.79,
      "end_seconds": 168.85,
      "duration_seconds": 3.06,
      "text": "Good. Is that good? ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0018",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 171.19,
      "end_seconds": 185.78,
      "duration_seconds": 14.59,
      "text": "That's good, yes. Now, you've had a bit of a history with the hep C itself, which we're still confirming has cleared. Any operations in the past?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0019",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 188.45,
      "end_seconds": 193.29,
      "duration_seconds": 4.84,
      "text": "Just my appendix out when I was a teenager."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0020",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 196.2,
      "end_seconds": 202.91,
      "duration_seconds": 6.71,
      "text": "And do you smoke? What do you do for a living?"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0021",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 203.82,
      "end_seconds": 213.61,
      "duration_seconds": 9.79,
      "text": "Never smoked in my life. I drive a delivery van, so it's a lot of sitting about."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0022",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 215.57,
      "end_seconds": 226.55,
      "duration_seconds": 10.98,
      "text": "That fits with the afternoon slump, partly. Tiredness after treatment is common, but I can't rule out an underactive thyroid yet."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0023",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 228.51,
      "end_seconds": 231.85,
      "duration_seconds": 3.34,
      "text": "Oh. Is that likely? ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0024",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 234.49,
      "end_seconds": 256.96,
      "duration_seconds": 22.47,
      "text": "Not especially, which is why it's only on my list rather than a diagnosis. I'd like to arrange blood tests, including the viral load to confirm the virus has cleared, and a thyroid check at the same draw."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0025",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 258.35,
      "end_seconds": 263.09,
      "duration_seconds": 4.74,
      "text": "Fine. Do I need to fast? ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0026",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 264.65,
      "end_seconds": 278.51,
      "duration_seconds": 13.86,
      "text": "No, you can eat normally. I'd also like to book an ultrasound of your liver, just to look at it properly after everything it's been through."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0027",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 279.63,
      "end_seconds": 285.28,
      "duration_seconds": 5.65,
      "text": "Right. And how long does all that take? ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0028",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 286.05,
      "end_seconds": 300.59,
      "duration_seconds": 14.54,
      "text": "The bloods come back within a week, and the scan will be booked by letter. You can do the bloods downstairs after this. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0029",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 303.33,
      "end_seconds": 308.94,
      "duration_seconds": 5.61,
      "text": "Okay. Anything I can do about the tired afternoons? ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0030",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 311.48,
      "end_seconds": 322.8,
      "duration_seconds": 11.32,
      "text": "Plan a short walk and a proper lunch break between deliveries, and try not to rely on sugary snacks to get you through."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0031",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 325.53,
      "end_seconds": 330.9,
      "duration_seconds": 5.37,
      "text": "That I can manage. What if it doesn't improve? ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0032",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 332.81,
      "end_seconds": 344.2,
      "duration_seconds": 11.39,
      "text": "If the tiredness isn't any better in six weeks, come back and see me and we'll look again."
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0033",
      "speaker_id": "person_1",
      "role": "PATIENT",
      "start_seconds": 346.11,
      "end_seconds": 353.12,
      "duration_seconds": 7.01,
      "text": "Right, will do. Thanks for explaining it all, the letter had me confused. ~"
    },
    {
      "segment_id": "SEG0034",
      "speaker_id": "person_2",
      "role": "DOCTOR",
      "start_seconds": 356.08,
      "end_seconds": 362.01,
      "duration_seconds": 5.93,
      "text": "Any time. Take care of yourself, and drive carefully. ~"
    }
  ]
}
